{"i":546,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Gus","text":"Ash is front. I called R, which is true. If Ash trusts me and steps R, he survives. If Hana counters, chaos might make Ash hesitate. I want Ash to survive this row so final three is Ash, Hana, me—then I can win jury favor by being honest guide. Countering my own true call would b"}
{"i":547,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"counter_call","name":"Hana","text":"Gus called R for Ash on the final row. Row 8's weak pane is unrevealed, so I must guess or trust the guide. If Gus tells truth, Ash survives; if lie, Ash falls. My choice affects only my survival if I am forced to step later, but here I am not walker. Wait to observe outcome and "}
{"i":552,"type":"thought","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","name":"Ash","text":"Row 8 is the last row; Guide Gus called R, but Guide may lie and rows are independent. Only three alive, so surviving is crucial; Gus's call is unverified and I have no pact with Gus. I'll trust the call since it is all I have, but no evidence supports it either way."}
{"i":555,"type":"stage_end","stage":"bridge","round":8,"phase":"crossing","survivors":["Ash","Gus","Hana"]}
